# Browser
# What a player sees of an attack that costs a land (CR 508.1h) under Bot2's Flooded Woodlands: the attackers dock says
# attacking Bot2 means sacrificing a land for each green creature, no "{0}". Bot1 has two Llanowar Elves and one land, so
# both Elves attacking can't be paid (CR 508.1j, 118.3) and the declaration is refused rather than asked again forever;
# one Elf attacks, Bot1 sacrifices the Forest for it, and Bot2 takes 1.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Llanowar Elves
Llanowar Elves
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Flooded Woodlands
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Flooded Woodlands.Cast
[T3 Bot1.BeginCombat]
Bot1.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Declare attackers
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Detail = 2 can attack  ·  attacking Bot2: sacrifice a land for each creature
! Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves#1 > Bot2; Llanowar Elves#2 > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Choose(Forest)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Graveyard = Forest
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves#2.Tapped = false
